In the case of `@InjectMock` I confirm we get to `ArcContainerImpl.mockObserversFor`:

```java
    private void mockObserversFor(String beanIdentifier, boolean mock) {
        for (InjectableObserverMethod<?> observer : observers) {
            if (observer instanceof Mockable && beanIdentifier.equals(observer.getDeclaringBeanIdentifier())) {
                Mockable mockable = (Mockable) observer;
                if (mock) {
                    mockable.arc$setMock(null);
                } else {
                    mockable.arc$clearMock();
                }
            }
        }
    }
```

And it finds the observer bean and calls `mockable.arc$setMock(null);` but I am not sure how this should disable the observer.

Considering this call runs the startup actions, and returns us what we need to install the mocks:

```java
            Method pushContext = runningQuarkusApplication.getClassLoader().loadClass(MockSupport.class.getName())
                    .getDeclaredMethod("pushContext");
            pushContext.setAccessible(true);
            pushContext
                    .invoke(null);
```

That's a pretty big chicken/egg problem.
